# 🔐 Cybersecurity Assessment Report

## 📋 Overview

This project presents a detailed cybersecurity assessment of system devices, drivers, and hardware components identified within a Windows environment.

The assessment focuses on **Device Anchors 601–610**, analyzing:

- Driver security posture
- Hardware attack surface
- Potential privilege escalation vectors
- Remote access risks
- USB-related threats
- Firmware and chipset vulnerabilities

The objective is to identify security weaknesses, evaluate risk levels, and provide actionable remediation recommendations.

---

## 🎯 Assessment Scope

The following components were analyzed:

| Anchor | Component |
|----------|------------|
| 601 | Intel PCI System Device |
| 602 | Remote Desktop Device Redirector (RDPBUS) |
| 603 | Intel Management Engine Interface |
| 604 | USB Root Hub (USB 3.0) |
| 605 | USB Composite Device |
| 606 | Intel USB 3.0 eXtensible Host Controller |
| 607 | Generic PnP Monitor |
| 608 | Generic PnP Monitor |
| 609 | Intel HD Graphics 630 |
| 610 | Intel HD Graphics 630 |

---

# 🚨 Executive Summary

The assessment identified multiple security concerns across drivers, remote access services, USB infrastructure, and firmware components.

## High-Risk Findings

### 🔴 Auto Logon Enabled
- Authentication bypass possible
